; set-nozzle-diameter
; Records which nozzle is installed after a nozzle change: diameter and type. The
; diameter step is the same one the filament load runs at its feed prompt - one call to
; hardware/confirm-nozzle-diameter.g: it asks with choice buttons (configured diameter
; preselected, "Other..." for a free value), persists a changed value per tool in
; sys/generated/nozzle<tool>.g via hardware/store-nozzle-diameter.g, offers
; filaments/<name>/nozzle-<key>.g when the loaded profile has none for the diameter
; (filament-profile/create-nozzle-file.g) and applies it with filament-profile/apply-nozzle-file.g. The type step
; (hardware/confirm-nozzle-type.g: brass, CHT, hardened, ...) persists to nozzle-type<tool>.g and
; is only asked here, not at filament load, because it selects no file. Cancelling
; either keeps the configured value. The nozzle belongs to the tool, not to the
; filament: the diameter selects, for every profile, the nozzle file and the calibration
; results (config-auto-pa-<key>.g, -nle-, -esteps-), <key> being the diameter with two
; decimals: 0.40, 1.20.
; Allowed while a print is paused (a nozzle swap after a clog), never while it prints.

if job.file.fileName != null && state.status != "paused"
  echo "Error: a print job is running - abort!"
  M99

var tool = min(max(state.currentTool, 0), 1)
M98 P"0:/sys/meltingplot/hardware/confirm-nozzle-diameter.g" T{var.tool}
M98 P"0:/sys/meltingplot/hardware/confirm-nozzle-type.g" T{var.tool}

; lib/format-number.g returns the key in global.result - read it straight away
M98 P"0:/sys/meltingplot/lib/format-number.g" F{global.nozzle_diameter[var.tool]} D2 W0
M291 R"Nozzle" P{"Tool " ^ var.tool ^ ": " ^ global.result ^ "mm " ^ global.nozzle_type[var.tool] ^ ". Check the Z offset and calibrate PA/NLE for this nozzle."} S1 T0
M400 ; sbc specific
